    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1019">

                <pb facs="1306" n="1296" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1296"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Registration/1–346: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-01-03T13:00:00+07:00">January 3, 1946—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 3—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. Strong representations have been made by Embassy to Foreign Minister,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d1019-f1"/> President of Legislative Yuan<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d1019-f2"/> and Minister of Economic Affairs<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d1019-f3"/> for modification of company law with particular
                    reference to definition of foreign corporation (re articles 7 and 292 revised
                    company law). Confidentially, as many top officials appear to be sympathetic
                    with our viewpoint, we are still hopeful of favorable action and do not consider
                    it advisable to appeal direct to Gimo (Generalissimo)<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d1019-f4"/> except as last resort. (Reference Dept’s 2076, December
                    28, 8 p.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d1019-f5"/>)</p>
                <p>Dr. Wong Wen-hao, Minister of Economic Affairs, assured us on January 2 that
                    deadline for registration of foreign companies would be postponed pending
                    promulgation of revised company law.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d1019-f6"/> (Sent to
                    Dept as 18, repeated Shanghai as 6 in reply to Shanghai’s No. 115, December
                        28.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d1019-f7"/>) Dr. Wong agreed to issue public
                    announcement to this effect.</p>
                <p>Request Commerce be advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f1" n="2" xml:id="d1019-f1-content">
