            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f2" n="3" xml:id="d1019-f2-content">
                <p>Sun Fo.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f3" n="4" xml:id="d1019-f3-content">
                <p>Wong Wen-hao.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f4" n="5" xml:id="d1019-f4-content">
                <p>Chiang Kai-shek, President of the National Government of the Republic of
                    China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f5" n="6" xml:id="d1019-f5-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1945v07#pg_1255">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1945, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">vii</hi>, p. 1255</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f6" n="7" xml:id="d1019-f6-content">
                <p>In telegram No. 174, January 28, the Counselor of Embassy in China reported that
                    the deadline for registration had been extended to the end of March (893.5034
                    Registration/1–2846).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1019-f7" n="8" xml:id="d1019-f7-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
